From: Studio (C1, claude/r4-content)
Subject: [PATCH 016] harness: the page up is the paged turn's LAST page and its card ref, as the seam keeps it (director13 S7)

director13's c4 stuck row 18 ("picture dikhao" redrew the card's bar) is the harness's own model of the seam, not
production. evals/hybrid-side-by-side.mjs passes the preselect only `avoid: shownScript`, and shownScript is the take of a
turn's FIRST page. Production's seam passes the page actually up — the LAST page of a paged turn (L.wbPrevPage) — and the ref
of the card that drew it (avoidRef = L.wbPrevRef), and pages with keep / keepRef. After row 16 (circle, then the card's bar)
the harness believed the circle was up, so the card's bar was a new board and no second view was picked.

This patch keeps shownRef beside shownScript, exactly as seam.js drawn() sets wbPrevRef; passes avoidRef to the preselect and
keep / keepRef to the paged check; and after a paged turn takes its last page and lastRef as the page up.
Measured on Brain's replay of director13 (tests/fixtures/replay.mjs, the harness's board-first sequence, no model calls):
  c4 stuck row 18: old → the card's bar, no second view; with 016 → round (the same whole as a circle)
  c5-t02 stuck row 20: old → the same "?" bars; with 016 (and Studio's S8) → wholes (two circles of 4 and 8 parts)
The seam itself already does this: replayed through it, both rows draw their second view on the run's tree 0dd31feb1.

